GnomeAI-RS for Debian
=====================

The package itself must be installed by an administrator, but both applications
run as the desktop user afterward. Runtime data and API keys are stored with
owner-only permissions under:

  ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/gnomeai-rs

No application command should be launched with sudo.

Applications
------------

The desktop menu contains:

* GnomeAI-RS Agent — terminal coding agent with /workspace, /provider and
  /websearch. The transcript supports mouse-wheel and keyboard scrolling.
  Hold the left mouse button while using the wheel to extend a selection
  beyond the viewport; releasing the button copies the selection.
* GnomeAI-RS WebTool — local browser interface at http://127.0.0.1:8787.

Equivalent commands:

  gnomeai-rs /path/to/workspace
  gnomeai-webtool

Firecrawl
---------

When Web Search is OFF, no Firecrawl process is started. With Web Search ON,
the first WebSearch/WebFetch request starts the bundled deployment through
rootless Podman. Its official container images are downloaded once into the
current user's Podman storage.

Useful diagnostics:

  gnomeai-firecrawl status
  gnomeai-firecrawl logs
  gnomeai-firecrawl stop

Podman is a recommended dependency because a remote Firecrawl URL can also be
configured instead. The local deployment binds only to 127.0.0.1:3002.

Provider account authentication
-------------------------------

OpenAI account authentication is owned by the bundled official Codex runtime.
Anthropic account authentication requires the official `claude` command.
Those account-backed modes are selected from the terminal agent. WebTool uses
API-backed providers, including the native Anthropic Messages API.
